Package: selectbench
Title: Compare Variable Selection Methods and Score Them Against the Truth
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jim", "Wang", email = "maojia.wang@mail.utoronto.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs several variable selection methods (forward, backward and
    bidirectional stepwise regression with AIC or BIC, the lasso with two
    common choices of the penalty, and best subset selection) on the same
    data and shows which variables each method picks, in one table and one
    plot. For simulated data in which the true variables are known, it also
    scores each method on how many true variables it finds and how many noise
    variables it picks up, and it can repeat this over many simulated data
    sets to compare the methods.
